    "## Exercise 4 – Expected Return Estimation\n",
    "### 4a \n",
    "Following the assignment, we use predicted excess returns from our preferred MA2 machine-learning model (Elastic Net) as estimates of $\\hat\\mu_t$. The fitted MA2 model, scaler, and feature definitions are loaded directly from the saved model bundle, and the preprocessing steps from MA2 are reproduced exactly to ensure consistency.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because characteristics observed in month $t$ are used to predict returns in month $t+1$, the resulting forecasts are shifted forward one month before entering the portfolio optimisation. If MA2 predictions are unavailable for a given stock-month, we fall back on a shrunk rolling historical mean of excess returns. This fallback is multiplied by a shrinkage factor of `MU_SHRINK = 0.05`, motivated by the mean-variance error-maximisation problem described by Michaud (1989) and related to the Bayes-Stein shrinkage approach of Jorion (1986). Shrinking the historical mean towards zero reduces estimation noise and produces more stable portfolio weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "02b93152",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MU_SHRINK = 0.05  # shrinkage applied ONLY to the historical-mean fallback (see text)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Load the fitted MA2 bundle (Elastic Net: preferred model in MA2) ----\n",
    "MA2_BUNDLE_PATH = \"/Users/AstridMoeller/Documents/GitHub/AEF-git/Aflevering2/ma2_elastic_net_bundle.joblib\"\n",
    "bundle          = joblib.load(MA2_BUNDLE_PATH)\n",
    "ma2_model       = bundle[\"model\"]\n",
    "ma2_scaler      = bundle[\"scaler\"]\n",
    "feature_columns = bundle[\"feature_columns\"]\n",
    "cont_feats      = bundle[\"continuous_features\"]\n",
    "stock_chars     = bundle[\"stock_chars\"]\n",
    "macro_vars      = bundle[\"macro_vars\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Load the characteristics panel MA2 was built from (same Absalon file) ----\n",
    "CHARS_FILE = \"/Users/AstridMoeller/AEF/data/stock_characteristics_monthly.parquet\"\n",
    "chars = pd.read_parquet(CHARS_FILE)\n",
    "chars[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(chars[\"date\"])\n",
    "chars = chars[[\"permno\", \"date\", \"sic2\"] + stock_chars + macro_vars].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Reproduce MA2 preprocessing exactly ----\n",
    "for col in stock_chars:                                    # monthly cross-sectional median\n",
    "    chars[col] = chars.groupby(\"date\")[col].transform(lambda x: x.fillna(x.median()))\n",
    "chars[macro_vars] = chars[macro_vars].ffill().bfill()      # macro: fill over time\n",
    "\n",
    "def recode_sic(sic):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(sic):\n",
    "        return \"Other\"\n",
    "    sic = int(sic)\n",
    "    if sic < 10:   return \"Agriculture\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 15: return \"Mining\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 18: return \"Construction\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 40: return \"Manufacturing\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 50: return \"Transportation\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 52: return \"Wholesale\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 60: return \"Retail\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 70: return \"Finance\"\n",
    "    elif sic < 90: return \"Services\"\n",
    "    else:          return \"Public Admin\"\n",
    "\n",
    "chars[\"sic_division\"] = chars[\"sic2\"].apply(recode_sic)\n",
    "\n",
    "for s in stock_chars:                                      # characteristic x macro interactions\n",
    "    for m in macro_vars:\n",
    "        chars[f\"{s}_x_{m}\"] = chars[s] * chars[m]\n",
    "\n",
    "sic_dummies = pd.get_dummies(chars[\"sic_division\"], prefix=\"sic\", drop_first=True, dtype=int)\n",
    "chars = pd.concat([chars, sic_dummies], axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# standardize continuous block with the SAVED MA2 scaler, align to MA2 column order\n",
    "chars[cont_feats] = ma2_scaler.transform(chars[cont_feats])\n",
    "X_chars = chars.reindex(columns=feature_columns, fill_value=0).fillna(0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "chars[\"mu_hat\"] = ma2_model.predict(X_chars)               # MA2 predicted excess return\n",
    "\n",
    "# features in month T predict the return of month T+1 -> shift to target month\n",
    "chars[\"target_month\"] = chars[\"date\"].dt.to_period(\"M\") + 1\n",
    "mu_by_month = {\n",
    "    period: g.set_index(\"permno\")[\"mu_hat\"]\n",
    "    for period, g in chars.groupby(\"target_month\")\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_ml_predicted_returns(date, available_permnos=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"MA2-predicted excess returns (Series indexed by permno) for holding month\n",
    "    `date`, or None if the month is not covered (-> historical-mean fallback).\"\"\"\n",
    "    return mu_by_month.get(pd.Timestamp(date).to_period(\"M\"))"
